<section class="fragment-plan" data-artifact="plan" data-slice="probe-engine-core" data-rev="3">
  <!-- @include-skip files-touched rows and callouts follow the sibling plan fragments' inline markup so the page renders them identically -->
  <table class="files-touched pl-files">
    <thead><tr><th>File</th><th>Status</th><th>Module</th><th>Lines</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">cli</span> crates/engine-cli/src/cli.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">Every short-help line over 80 columns under -h is shortened by one rule (47 lines on 10 surfaces at HEAD 89fe959), and two possible-value lists move to the long help. resume --json states that the extension is replaced by .jsonl. The hidden test seam calibrate --inject-failure is added.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>crates/engine-cli/src</td><td>+66 / -47</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">test</span> crates/engine-cli/tests/cli_args.rs, schemas.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">The 80-column test reads -h and --help on all 10 help surfaces (20 checks). Regression tests cover the dump path, one OS-error mention, and no escape byte on redirected stderr. Failure-record tests for simulate and bench, and calibration drives with the injected failure, are validated against the record schemas. Negative schema checks refuse the word failure and a missing error key.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>crates/engine-cli/tests</td><td>+210 / -9</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">domain</span> crates/engine/src/error.rs, observe/mod.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">The calibration classifier moves into the engine error type with the same values, plus error.code and error.retriable. FailureRecord carries the envelope, the correlation keys, outcome error, and the three error keys, and no statistic key. MatchFigures gains the two optional error keys.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>crates/engine/src</td><td>+115</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">cli</span> crates/engine-cli/src/main.rs, bench.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">When simulate or bench fails, the command prints one failure record on stdout, then the prose line on stderr, and exits 1. The other subcommands keep prose only. The bench --matches check returns a typed configuration error.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>crates/engine-cli/src</td><td>+42 / -4</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">cli</span> crates/engine-cli/src/calibrate/worker.rs, calibrate/mod.rs, report/mod.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">Calibration writes outcome error in place of failure, on a failed match and on a run with a failed worker, with error.type, error.code, and error.retriable. The injected failure is forwarded to shard 0 only.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>crates/engine-cli/src</td><td>+62 / -17</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">contract</span> schemas/observability/match-stats and run-report</summary><div class="pl-card">outcome accepts success or error only. The statistic and benchmark keys are required only on a record that is not an error, and an error record requires the three error keys. The envelope and correlation keys stay required.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>schemas/observability</td><td>—</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">docs</span> docs/reference/cli.md, README.md</summary><div class="pl-card">The simulate, bench, and calibrate sections of the command reference, and one README sentence, state what a failed run prints and that it exits 1.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>README.md and docs/reference</td><td>+8</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <div class="pl-risks">
    <aside class="callout callout-warn"><strong>Calibration output changes after its verification (medium).</strong> The failed-match record and the run report change their word to error and gain two keys. The product owner accepted this: earlier run folders are not a compatibility target.</aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-warn"><strong>An error run report without the error keys (medium).</strong> After the schema change an error record without the three error keys is refused. Step 10 adds them, and the injected worker failure drives the path against the real schema.</aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-info"><strong>The injected failure leaks into a real run (low).</strong> The calibrate test seam is hidden, off by default, and applies to shard 0 only; a test asserts it stays out of the help.</aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-info"><strong>Help text keeps growing (low).</strong> Later slices took the over-width count from 9 options to 47 lines. Step 1 applies a rule, and the widened test fails the gate if a later option makes a line longer than 80 columns.</aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-info"><strong>Stdout consumers of a failed run (low).</strong> The exit code stays 1, and the command reference and the README state what a failed run prints.</aside>
  </div>
